# Pipeline code

Read `process/docs/AI-GUIDE.md` before editing these files.

- Fix the module that maps the Figma property. Do not patch generated `bricks.json`.
- A component the layer name does not say is still a candidate when its children share a shape (`process/modules/recognize-parts/structure.mjs`). Name regex stays a hint. Do not add a file-specific name regex.
- No whack-a-mole. A failed file is not a new regex. Check the same shape in the catalog and in another section, then change the shared rule and add a test. Picture (Figma render or headless Playwright) plus tree. The next file has to pass without another special case.
- A new or changed rule gets a test in `process/test/` that uses the real Figma number. Then `npm test --prefix process`.
- A constant comes from `tree.md` or `raw.json`. Put the measurement next to it in a comment. No guessed default.
- A Figma property that is not in `process/modules/property-coverage/handling.json` is classified there first (`read`, `ignored`, `limit`, or `gap`).
- After a render or decide change, run `node process/modules/maintenance/rebuild-diff.mjs <fileKey>` before any push. A section you did not mean to change means the rule is wrong.
- Check the other side of a symmetric fix (top/bottom, x/y, desktop/breakpoint) and grep every writer of that setting (`render/`, `responsive/merge.mjs`, verify).

```javascript
// BAD: edit the generated template
// bricks.json settings._typography["font-size"] = "16px"

// GOOD: map the Figma font size in process/modules/write-bricks/render/, test that number, rebuild-diff
```
